# nr-office-comrs-pswire: the PowerShell value semantics of mixdog-office-com (src/ps/, tests/pswire.rs). Applied by the wave's wiring.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/src/lib.rs
After `pub mod identity;` (the module list at the top), add:
    pub mod ps;
(the module is public: tests/pswire.rs and the later host ports reach it as `mixdog_office_com::ps`).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/Cargo.toml
[dependencies], after `mixdog-rt = { workspace = true }`:
    regex = { workspace = true }
(src/ps/text.rs: -match, -replace and -split run on the regex crate; `regex = "1.12.3"` is already a workspace dependency, locked at 1.13.1.)

New section, after [dev-dependencies] ... before [features]:
    # src/ps/collate.rs (CompareStringEx with the user's locale: Sort-Object and -eq on strings), src/ps/datetime.rs
    # (TzSpecificLocalTimeToSystemTimeEx with the dynamic time zone: ToUniversalTime) and tests/pswire.rs (the zone key name).
    [target.'cfg(windows)'.dependencies]
    windows-sys = { workspace = true, features = ["Win32_Foundation", "Win32_Globalization", "Win32_System_Time"] }

After the `[[test]] name = "twin_detect"` block, add (the crate has autotests = false):
    [[test]]
    name = "pswire"
    path = "tests/pswire.rs"

## native/core/Cargo.lock
The package `mixdog-office-com` gains the two edges `regex` and `windows-sys 0.61.2` in its dependencies list (alphabetical:
"regex" after "mixdog-workspace-hack", "windows-sys 0.61.2" after "tokio-util"). Both are already in the lock (regex 1.13.1,
windows-sys 0.61.2): regenerate offline with `cargo metadata --offline --manifest-path native/core/Cargo.toml`.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml
Feature unification only: regenerate with `cargo hakari generate` if the lead's flow does so (regex default features,
windows-sys features Win32_Foundation, Win32_Globalization, Win32_System_Time).

## What this task registers
No protocol method, no service, nothing in SERVICE_PENDING. The module is a library for the host ports of the track
(nr-office-comrs-*): `ps::payload::parse_payload` for each request line, `ps::json::emit_json` for each answer line,
`ps::fingerprint::snapshot_fingerprint` for the snapshot fingerprint, and the casts, sort and text helpers.

## Run notes for the lead
tests/pswire.rs (not #[ignore]) reads tests/fixtures/pswire/corpus.json: every entry must pass on Windows. The UTC text of a
date is compared only when the machine's time zone key name equals the corpus' (Korea Standard Time). `pswire_live` is
#[ignore]: it runs recorder/pswire-corpus.ps1 (Windows PowerShell 5.1, no Office) and is for the reviewer on a Korean and an
English Windows.
